    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the acceptance test passes. The audit log confirms the unified format: `memberId=NSW2616E6609E3` (`NSW` + `26` + `16E6609E` + `3`).\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. Each piece of logic landed where it belongs:\n\n**Identity generation (`service/`)**\n- Renamed `CustomerCodeGenerator` \u2192 **`MemberIdGenerator`**: now formats `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, taking the fiscal year as a parameter and computing the trailing Luhn `CHK` over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`. It keeps the same SHA-256-over-`(normalizedTelephone+lastName)` first-8-upper-hex `HASH8` used by the region-and-hash identity.\n- Renamed `CustomerCodeDeduplicator` \u2192 **`MemberIdDeduplicator`**: collision handling now applies to the `memberId`.\n\n**Model (`model/`)**\n- `Owner`: field `customerCode` \u2192 `memberId` (column `customer_code` \u2192 `member_id`).\n- Replaced `CheckDigit` (which was owner/customerCode-coupled) with a small, reusable **`Luhn`** utility exposing just `checkDigit(String)`; the generator reuses it. Deleted `MembershipNumber` and `CheckDigit`.\n- `Locality.fromCustomerCode` \u2192 `fromMemberId`, extracting the region as the leading letter run before the two-digit FY.\n\n**Wiring / consumers**\n- `ClinicServiceImpl.saveOwner`: derives the FY from the registration date and generates/dedups the `memberId`.\n- `OwnerMapper`: dropped the `membershipNumber`/`checkDigit` mappings; `memberId` maps directly; `formatLocality` (and thus `ownerSegment`) now reads from `memberId`; reverse mapping ignores `memberId`.\n- `OwnerCreatedEvent` + `OwnerAuditLogger`: the audit record now carries `memberId`.\n- `openapi.yml`: replaced the three schema fields with a single documented `memberId`.\n- Renamed the column and widened it (`VARCHAR(32)`) across all four DB schemas.\n\n`./mvnw test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
